ArchiveEntry "F-fold F3a (no synchronized equilibrium: |M|>Vg => angle velocity sign-definite)"

/* F-fold = the limit-cycle saddle-node (loss-of-sync) boundary.  Its full formalization
 * (periodic orbits + Floquet) is beyond current provers (Mathlib etc. lack the theory) --
 * F1/F2 are left to validated numerics, honestly.  The CERTIFIABLE sub-block is F3's
 * algebraic core (R2/Sigma_2-type, same family as R2_fold.kyx / R2real_fold.kyx):
 *
 * The synchronizing angle balance has the form  theta' = M - Vg*sin(theta)  (M the net
 * unbalance forcing, Vg>0 the max restoring).  Encode sin via s with s^2<=1.  CLAIM: if the
 * forcing exceeds the maximum restoring torque (M>Vg>0) then theta' = M - Vg*s > 0 for ALL
 * admissible s -- the angle velocity is strictly sign-definite, has NO zero (no equilibrium),
 * so theta drifts monotonically and unboundedly: loss of synchronization. */
Problem
  \forall M \forall Vg \forall s
  ( M > Vg & Vg > 0 & s^2 <= 1 -> M - Vg*s > 0 )
End.
Tactic "no equilibrium => sign-definite drift by QE" QE End.
End.

ArchiveEntry "F-fold F3b (synchronized equilibrium exists iff |M|<=Vg: the fold boundary)"

/* The complementary R2-type statement pinning the boundary: a synchronized angle
 * equilibrium (theta' = 0, i.e. M = Vg*sin(theta), encoded M = Vg*s with s^2<=1) exists iff
 * the forcing is within the restoring envelope, M^2 <= Vg^2.  Past it (M^2>Vg^2) F3a gives
 * unbounded drift.  This is the equilibrium-level fold Sigma_fold|_{angle}; the genuine
 * limit-cycle fold sits past Sigma_H and is the validated-numerics part. */
Problem
  \forall M \forall Vg
  ( Vg > 0 ->
    ( ( \exists s ( s^2 <= 1 & M = Vg*s ) ) <-> M^2 <= Vg^2 ) )
End.
Tactic "equilibrium exists iff within envelope by QE" QE End.
End.
